    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "zmc9whe00dqw",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Exploring the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "lio8gdbbws8o",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "p9tghk8lsi0v"
              ],
              "text": "Dakhla Oasis"
            },
            {
              "_key": "b14c71v38402",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ": A Journey Through the Heart of Egypt "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "p9tghk8lsi0v",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58783",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "In the captivating Dakhla Oasis, nestled in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt’s Western Desert"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", transportation weaves a unique tapestry of local life, connecting the myriad of small settlements and historic sites. The primary modes of transit here are crowded pick-ups and microbuses, each a tiny universe bustling with activity. However, newcomers might find the routes and destinations of these vehicles somewhat enigmatic."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Western_Desert_(Egypt)",
              "newTab": true
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "For those adventurous souls aiming to visit the ancient town of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000008"
              ],
              "text": "Al Qasr"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", known for its well-preserved mudbrick architecture, your journey begins at Sharia As Sawra Al Khadra. Here, amidst the lively hum of daily life, you’ll find pick-ups ready to transport you into the past. Likewise, journeys to Balat, with its impressive "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000b"
              ],
              "text": "necropolis"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", and Bashendi, a gateway to stunning landscapes, commence from the bustling area in front of the local hospital."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-qasr-village/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/bahariya-oasis/al-qasr-village",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/necropolis-of-anfushi/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/alexandria/necropolis-of-anfushi",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000013",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Most microbuses, the lifeline of local transport, radiate from the servees station located on Sharia Tamir. These are the veins through which the daily rhythm of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000010"
              ],
              "text": "Dakhla"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " pulses. On occasion, you might find it more convenient to negotiate a ‘special’ pick-up. This option allows for a more personalized journey, tailored to your itinerary and pace."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/deir-el-hagar/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/dakhla-oasis/deir-el-hagar",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "However, there’s an alternative that marries convenience with the thrill of exploration: hiring a taxi to Al Qasr. This choice offers a blend of comfort and flexibility, with the added benefit of having a local driver who knows the landscape intimately. Expect to pay around LE100 for this service, which generally includes waiting time, giving you the freedom to "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000015"
              ],
              "text": "wander"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " through Al Qasr’s maze of history before returning to the present."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/rosetta-rasheed-travel-guide/wandering-through/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/rosetta-rasheed-travel-guide/wandering-through/",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "In updating this travel narrative, any outdated information has been revised to reflect the current state of transportation in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001a"
              ],
              "text": "Dakhla Oasis"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". As you embark on your journey through this enchanting part of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001d"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", each mode of transport offers not just a ride, but a window into the everyday life and rich history of this remarkable region."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/history-of-dakhla-oasis/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/dakhla-oasis/history-of-dakhla-oasis",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001d",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/qasr-ibrim/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/abu-simbel/qasr-ibrim",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000021",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Dakhla Oasis Travel Guide"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000023",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Dakhla-e1554945660393-1200x900-1.jpg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "dakhla oasis travel guide"
            }
          ],
          "caption": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "Weathered elegance: a balcony stands defiantly amidst the crumbling relics of a bygone era"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/dakhla-oasis-trips-in-egypt.jpg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "dakhla oasis travel guide"
            }
          ],
          "caption": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "The historic minaret of the Nasr El Din Mosque rises over the Dakhla Oasis, embodying the enduring spirit of Egypt's heartland deserts"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000025",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Essential Egypt Travel Tips: Your Guide to a Seamless Journey"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000027",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Navigate your Egyptian "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000029",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000028"
              ],
              "text": "adventure"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " with confidence using our essential travel tips. From navigating local customs to selecting the best times to visit iconic sites, our guide ensures you make the most of your trip. Click for insider advice on experiencing Egypt like a pro!"
